Stormbringer is indeed a demon. It is not chaotic nor lawful nor neutral,
actually, but a creature against them all... in the book, Stormbringer
actually caused the world to cease to exist. Only the sword still existed
after 'Armageddon'.... I've read the statistics of the sword from the
RPG Stormbringer. It gives the sword so much power... listed:
 - the sword can control itself if it wants...
 - the sword controls the user not the opposite
 - the sword kills anything
 - the sword is just about immune to all damage
 - the sword gives the wielder (if it wants) SO much power
   that the wielder can beat gods... if the Stormbringer wants...

Well, put it simple, the sword in Nethack has about 0.0001% of it's real
power in the novel Stormbringer or as described in the RPG.
  
-Marko

BTW. The main power that the sword has COULD be implemented to the game.
The sword hits ALWAYS and always a die roll of d100 is substracted from
the enemy's int. If int falls below or to zero, the victim dies automatically.
The sword absorbs the int points and the wielder can use them later.
a nice thing, don't you think?



